<p>Returns a resource from a 2DA.
</p>
<div class="dascript" style="font-family:monospace; background-color:#F9F9F9; border: 1px dashed #2F6FAB; white-space:pre; line-height:1.25em; padding:1.0em;"><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Resource%20keyword" title="Resource keyword">resource</a> GetM2DAResource(<br />    <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Int%20keyword" title="Int keyword">int</a> n2DA,<br />    <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/String%20keyword" title="String keyword">string</a> sColumn,<br />    <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Int%20keyword" title="Int keyword">int</a> nRow,<br />    <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/String%20keyword" title="String keyword">string</a> s2da&#160;= ""<br />);</div>
<dl>
<dt>Parameters:
<dd><dl><dt style="font-weight:normal; font-style:italic;">n2DA<dd>The 2DA to access<dt style="font-weight:normal; font-style:italic;">sColumn<dd>The name of the column to access<dt style="font-weight:normal; font-style:italic;">nRow<dd>The 0 based index of the row to access<dt style="font-weight:normal; font-style:italic;">s2da<dd>(optional) if n2da is -1 and this is a valid resource, it will retrieve the 2da based on the name instead of the index. Note that this should be avoided when possible.
</dl>
</dl><dl><dt>Returns:
<p><dd>Returns a resrouce specified by the parameters.
</p>
</dl><dl><dt>Source:
<p><dd><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Script.ldf" title="Script.ldf">script.ldf</a>
</p>
</dl>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Description">Description</span></h2>
<p>Returns a 2DA resource on the specified Row and Column values.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Remarks">Remarks</span></h2>
<p>Note that nRow is the value in the ID field of the row you wish to access.
</p>
